SUBJECT: constant.pm, UNITCHECK and pre 5.10
FROM: Nicholas Clark 
BODY: I'd like to made the following change to constant.pm before merging the current version for 5.8.9, because I don't feel comfortable about changing the state of UNITCHECK in a core release point upgrade. The change to t/constant.t seemed to be the cleanest way to test it. Nicholas Clark --- lib/constant.pm.orig Tue Nov 6 01:26:03 yeartoken +++ lib/constant.pm Fri Nov 16 14:35:45 yeartoken @@ -9,7 +9,8 @@ $VERSION = '1.12'; #======================================================================= # Some names are evil choices. -my %keywords = map +($_, 1), qw{ BEGIN INIT CHECK UNITCHECK END DESTROY AUTOLOAD }; +my %keywords = map +($_, 1), qw{ BEGIN INIT CHECK END DESTROY AUTOLOAD }; +$keywords{UNITCHECK}++ if $] > 5.009; my %forced_into_main = map +($_, 1), qw{ STDIN STDOUT STDERR ARGV ARGVOUT ENV INC SIG }; --- t/constant.t.orig Tue Nov 6 01:26:03 yeartoken +++ t/constant.t Fri Nov 16 14:44:49 yeartoken @@ -220,6 +220,12 @@ my @Expected_Warnings = qr/^Constant name 'SIG' is forced into package main:: at/, ); +unless ($] > 5.009) { + # Remove the UNITCHECK warning + $Expected_Warnings[4] = qr/^$/; + splice @warnings, 4, 0, ""; +} + # when run under "make test" if (@warnings == 16) { push @warnings, "";

